# Build artifacts from `tree-sitter test`/`parse`, which compiles the parser in place.
node_modules/
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.wasm

# `src/parser.c`, `src/grammar.json` and `src/node-types.json` are deliberately NOT ignored. They are
# generated, and committing generated files is usually wrong — but tree-sitter consumers (Neovim, Helix,
# GitHub's linguist) build from `src/parser.c` without running `tree-sitter generate`, so a repository
# without it is unusable to exactly the audience this grammar exists for. `src/tags.h` is committed for the
# same reason, and `npm run check:tags` is what keeps it honest.
